name: batcat
description: A cat(1) clone with syntax highlighting and Git integration.
usage:
- 'Usage: batcat [OPTIONS] [FILE]...'
- '       batcat <COMMAND>'
positionals:
- name: FILE
  variadic: true
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- name: COMMAND
  required: true
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
flags:
- spellings:
  - -A
  - --show-all
  description: Show non-printable characters like space, tab or newline. This option can also be used to print binary files. Use '--tabs' to control the width of the tab-placeholders.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --nonprintable-notation
  value_name: <notation>
  value_kind: Required
  choices:
  - name: unicode
    description: (␇, ␊, ␀, ..)
  - name: caret
    description: (^G, ^J, ^@, ..)
  description: Set notation for non-printable characters.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -p
  - --plain
  value_name: '...'
  value_kind: Required
  description: Only show plain style, no decorations. This is an alias for '--style=plain'. When '-p' is used twice ('-pp'), it also disables automatic paging (alias for '--style=plain --paging=never').
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -l
  - --language
  value_name: <language>
  value_kind: Required
  description: Explicitly set the language for syntax highlighting. The language can be specified as a name (like 'C++' or 'LaTeX') or possible file extension (like 'cpp', 'hpp' or 'md'). Use '--list-languages' to show all supported language names and file extensions.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -H
  - --highlight-line
  value_name: <N:M>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Highlight the specified line ranges with a different background color For example: ''--highlight-line 40'' highlights line 40 ''--highlight-line 30:40'' highlights lines 30 to 40 ''--highlight-line :40'' highlights lines 1 to 40 ''--highlight-line 40:'' highlights lines 40 to the end of the file ''--highlight-line 30:+10'' highlights lines 30 to 40'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --file-name
  value_name: <name>
  value_kind: Required
  description: Specify the name to display for a file. Useful when piping data to bat from STDIN when bat does not otherwise know the filename. Note that the provided file name is also used for syntax detection.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -d
  - --diff
  description: Only show lines that have been added/removed/modified with respect to the Git index. Use --diff-context=N to control how much context you want to see.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --diff-context
  value_name: <N>
  value_kind: Required
  description: Include N lines of context around added/removed/modified lines when using '--diff'.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --tabs
  value_name: <T>
  value_kind: Required
  description: Set the tab width to T spaces. Use a width of 0 to pass tabs through directly
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --wrap
  value_name: <mode>
  value_kind: Required
  description: Specify the text-wrapping mode (*auto*, never, character). The '--terminal-width' option can be used in addition to control the output width.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -S
  - --chop-long-lines
  description: Truncate all lines longer than screen width. Alias for '--wrap=never'.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --terminal-width
  value_name: <width>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Explicitly set the width of the terminal instead of determining it automatically. If prefixed with ''+'' or ''-'', the value will be treated as an offset to the actual terminal width. See also: ''--wrap''.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -n
  - --number
  description: Only show line numbers, no other decorations. This is an alias for '--style=numbers'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --color
  value_name: <when>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Specify when to use colored output. The automatic mode only enables colors if an interactive terminal is detected - colors are automatically disabled if the output goes to a pipe. Possible values: *auto*, never, always.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --italic-text
  value_name: <when>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Specify when to use ANSI sequences for italic text in the output. Possible values: always, *never*.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --decorations
  value_name: <when>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Specify when to use the decorations that have been specified via ''--style''. The automatic mode only enables decorations if an interactive terminal is detected. Possible values: *auto*, never, always.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -f
  - --force-colorization
  description: Alias for '--decorations=always --color=always'. This is useful if the output of bat is piped to another program, but you want to keep the colorization/decorations.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --paging
  value_name: <when>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Specify when to use the pager. To disable the pager, use --paging=never'' or its alias,''-P''. To disable the pager permanently, set BAT_PAGING to ''never''. To control which pager is used, see the ''--pager'' option. Possible values: *auto*, never, always.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --pager
  value_name: <command>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Determine which pager is used. This option will override the PAGER and BAT_PAGER environment variables. The default pager is ''less''. To control when the pager is used, see the ''--paging'' option. Example: ''--pager "less -RF"''.'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -m
  - --map-syntax
  value_name: <glob:syntax>
  value_kind: Required
  description: Map a glob pattern to an existing syntax name. The glob pattern is matched on the full path and the filename. For example, to highlight *.build files with the Python syntax, use -m '*.build:Python'. To highlight files named '.myignore' with the Git Ignore syntax, use -m '.myignore:Git Ignore'. Note that the right-hand side is the *name* of the syntax, not a file extension.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --ignored-suffix
  value_name: <ignored-suffix>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Ignore extension. For example: ''bat --ignored-suffix ".dev" my_file.json.dev'' will use JSON syntax, and ignore ''.dev'''
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --theme
  value_name: <theme>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Set the theme for syntax highlighting. Use ''--list-themes'' to see all available themes. To set a default theme, add the ''--theme="..."'' option to the configuration file or export the BAT_THEME environment variable (e.g.: export BAT_THEME="...").'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --list-themes
  description: Display a list of supported themes for syntax highlighting.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --style
  value_name: <components>
  value_kind: Required
  choices:
  - name: default
    description: enables recommended style components (default).
  - name: full
    description: enables all available components.
  - name: auto
    description: same as 'default', unless the output is piped.
  - name: plain
    description: disables all available components.
  - name: changes
    description: show Git modification markers.
  - name: header
    description: alias for 'header-filename'.
  - name: header-filename
    description: show filenames before the content.
  - name: header-filesize
    description: show file sizes before the content.
  - name: grid
    description: vertical/horizontal lines to separate side bar and the header from the content.
  - name: rule
    description: horizontal lines to delimit files.
  - name: numbers
    description: show line numbers in the side bar.
  - name: snip
    description: draw separation lines between distinct line ranges.
  description: 'Configure which elements (line numbers, file headers, grid borders, Git modifications, ..) to display in addition to the file contents. The argument is a comma-separated list of components to display (e.g. ''numbers,changes,grid'') or a pre-defined style (''full''). To set a default style, add the ''--style=".."'' option to the configuration file or export the BAT_STYLE environment variable (e.g.: export BAT_STYLE="..").'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -r
  - --line-range
  value_name: <N:M>
  value_kind: Required
  description: 'Only print the specified range of lines for each file. For example: ''--line-range 30:40'' prints lines 30 to 40 ''--line-range :40'' prints lines 1 to 40 ''--line-range 40:'' prints lines 40 to the end of the file ''--line-range 40'' only prints line 40 ''--line-range 30:+10'' prints lines 30 to 40'
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -L
  - --list-languages
  description: Display a list of supported languages for syntax highlighting.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -u
  - --unbuffered
  description: This option exists for POSIX-compliance reasons ('u' is for 'unbuffered'). The output is always unbuffered - this option is simply ignored.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --diagnostic
  description: Show diagnostic information for bug reports.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - --acknowledgements
  description: Show acknowledgements.
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -h
  - --help
  description: Print help (see a summary with '-h')
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
- spellings:
  - -V
  - --version
  description: Print version
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
provenance:
  sources:
  - help-text
  confidence: 0.5
children_filled: true
